Now audio.js. Needs robust WebAudio synth with music.

Design:
```js
class AudioEngine {
 constructor(){ this.ctx=null; this.master=null; this.musicGain=null; this.sfxGain=null; this.enabled=true; this.musicMode=null; this.timer=null; this.step=0; this.nextTime=0; this.intensity=0;}
 init(){ if ctx return; create; ... start scheduler }
 setEnabled(bool)
 setMusic(mode)
 play(name, opts)
 tone(...) etc
}
```
Music scheduler uses lookahead scheduling with setInterval 120ms; must be cleared on mode change. Patterns per mode:

menu: ambient arpeggio at 100 BPM, chords minor: A minor (A2 bass, arpeggio A4 C5 E5 G5), F, C, G. Use sine/triangle pads, soft.

battle: 152 BPM, driving: bass eighth notes root, kick/hat noise, lead motif. Create sequences of semitone offsets.

Implement noteFreq(n) using 440*2^((n-69)/12) with MIDI numbers.

Scheduler:
```
_schedule() {
 if(!ctx || !enabled) return;
 const ahead = 0.15;
 while(nextTime < ctx.currentTime + 0.2) {
   this._playStep(step, nextTime, mode);
   nextTime += stepDur;
   step++;
 }
}
```
If disabled, still advance? pause music when disabled. On setEnabled false, stop interval & cancel scheduled nodes? Use musicGain.gain to 0 and stop scheduler. To be safe, store active nodes? Simpler: musicGain to 0, scheduler keeps scheduling silent notes — CPU minor. Instead stop scheduler when disabled and restart when enabled.

SFX:
- hit(damage, kind): low sine thump + noise burst filtered.
- ko: big noise + sub drop, maybe crowd swell = filtered noise 1.2s.
- jump, doubleJump, land, shield, shieldBreak, dodge, whoosh, projectile type fire/zap/ice/seed, counter, beep, go, game, menu hover/click, charge loop? We can trigger charge sound at intervals from game; skip.

Audio autoplay: init on first pointerdown/keydown globally, main sets.

Noise buffer create once.

Music melody arrays:
battle bass: [0,0,null,7,0,0,10,7] over A minor? Use MIDI roots [45,45,43,41] per bar. Lead pattern maybe pentatonic.

Let's write concise but effective.

For SFX, use multiple oscillators with gain envelopes.

Careful about volume: master 0.6, music 0.16, sfx 0.55.

Also a "crowd" ambient? skip.

Add `duck` function? no.

Write audio.js.

